  {
    "id": "p1791733948641-0",
    "place": "KTM MOTOHALL",
    "region": "",
    "date": "2026-10-10",
    "story": "It was a cold, rainy day, and a heavy grey atmosphere hung over the event. While most would see bad weather, I saw a dramatic backdrop. Sitting quietly under a white canopy was the KTM Super Duke R, affectionately known as \"The Beast.\"\n\nWhat struck me immediately was the contrast: KTM's iconic orange—a color forged through decades of championship racing and engineering history right here in Mattighofen—cutting sharply through the wet, gloomy scene.\n\nI took a low-angle shot to highlight the aggressive stance of the rear wheel and its reflection on the rain-soaked asphalt. For me, this photo isn't just about a motorcycle; it captures the raw essence of KTM—unapologetic power, racing legacy, and readiness to conquer any condition, wet or dry.",
    "type": "photo",
    "image": "assets/photos/ktm-motohall-1791733948641-0.jpg",
    "thumb": "assets/photos/ktm-motohall-1791733948641-0-thumb.jpg"
  },
